{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"plan","namespace":"","artifact_type":"","name":"P9e17b896"},"owner_reference":"#3276","content":"{\"plan_id\":\"P9e17b896\",\"feature\":\"contract-verification-async-reporting\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"goal\":\"Make bare Agent()-dispatched dh agents deliver their findings through a durable backend destination instead of a synchronous return value, at both defect sites (contract-verification/implement-feature step 4a, and groom/error.md's Agent Failure procedure), and stop dispatch-contract/SKILL.md from authorizing the anti-pattern that regenerates it.\",\"context\":\"# Plan Context \\u2014 #3276 Contract-Verification Async Reporting\\n\\n## The defect in one paragraph\\n\\nUnder this runtime's dispatch semantics, a bare non-team `Agent()` call returns only a\\n\\\"Spawned successfully\\\" acknowledgment \\u2014 the subagent's plain-text output is never visible to\\nthe dispatcher. Three files encode the opposite assumption. `agents/contract-verification.md:151`\\nsays \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \\u2014 you register no artifact and\\nwrite no task state.\\\" `skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` lines 187-198 branch on that\\nnever-arriving value. `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md` step 3\\ndispatches `dh:task-worker` asking it to \\\"Report: last_success, first_failure, failure_type\\\" and\\nfeeds those into a Mermaid decision tree at lines 30-40 that can therefore never reach its\\nEscalation branch. `skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md:11` is the doctrine authorizing the pattern.\\n\\nThere is no error, no timeout, no blocked state. \\\"No violations found\\\" is byte-for-byte\\nindistinguishable from \\\"the finding was dropped.\\\" That silence is why this is P2.\\n\\n## The fix pattern (same pattern, deliberately different destinations)\\n\\nEach agent writes its own result to a backend destination named in its own agent file; the\\nconsumer reads it back. Per `skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`'s `<result_destination>` primary\\nrule \\u2014 \\\"Put your result where your own agent file says\\\" \\u2014 this resolves routing before the\\nartifact fallback is ever reached.\\n\\nThe two sites use different destinations because their consumption shapes differ:\\n\\n- **contract-verification \\u2192 `backlog_groom` on the Concerns section.** Accumulating, human-facing,\\n  actionable checklist items, consumed much later by `/complete-implementation`. Same shape as\\n  every other concern already flowing into that section. Architect \\u00a71.1 explicitly rejects\\n  `artifact_register` here: no `artifact_type` enum member fits, and `code-review` is already\\n  owned by `dh:code-reviewer`.\\n- **groom/error.md diagnostic \\u2192 `artifact_register`.** Single-shot structured diagnostic data\\n  feeding one immediate decision \\u2014 the T0/TN shape, not the checklist shape.\\n\\nForcing one mechanism onto both sites would be the over-generalization Impact Radius R5 warns\\nagainst.\\n\\n## Hard exclusions (all four are traps this item has already walked into)\\n\\n1. **Never `TeamCreate`.** Explicitly ruled out by the user. Both sites stay bare `Agent()` spawns.\\n2. **Never `SendMessage(to=\\\"team-lead\\\", ...)`.** There is no team-lead when there is no team. This\\n   is #3249's fix for `impact-analyst` and it is NOT transferable \\u2014 `impact-analyst` is a\\n   `TeamCreate` teammate. It is the most discoverable wrong answer.\\n3. **Never re-introduce SendMessage as transport at all.** Commit `11082f0eb` removed it\\n   deliberately: SendMessage is Claude-Code-only, and this plugin's content also targets Codex,\\n   OpenCode, Crush and Kilo.\\n4. **Never touch #3250's scope.** #3250 audits TeamCreate teammates missing a\\n   SendMessage-to-team-lead step. The two items must remain independently verifiable (AC5).\\n\\n## Files, and only these files\\n\\n| File | Task | Change |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md` | T1 | New `issue_number` input; Output Format rewritten to `backlog_groom`; drop unused `SendMessage` grant |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` | T1 | Add `Issue number: {issue}` to step 4a's dispatch prompt; delete the synchronous branch at lines 187-198 |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md` | T2 | Diagnostic agent registers a YAML `audit-report` artifact; read-back inserted before the decision tree |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` | T2 | One table row \\u2014 `audit-report` ownership now names two producers |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md` | T3 | Split the conflated sentence at line 11; keep specialist-selection, delete the reporting claim |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` | T4 | **VERIFY UNCHANGED.** Architect \\u00a75 confirms no edit needed |\\n\\n## Explicitly deferred (architect \\u00a77 \\u2014 do not fold in)\\n\\n- A general documentation-and-review gate requiring all `dh:*` agents to declare a completion-report\\n  step, plus a follow-up audit of the remaining ~4 agents named in the frequency analysis. Not in\\n  this item's five Acceptance Criteria; belongs in a separate follow-up item.\\n- `skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \\u2014 independently verified clean (zero bare `Agent(` calls,\\n  already artifact-register-based). Correct pattern. Do not touch.\\n\\n## Decomposition decisions\\n\\n**Why T1 merges the producer and the consumer.** Splitting them produces an incorrect intermediate\\nstate in either order: land the agent edit alone and BOTH the agent and step 4a write each concern\\n(duplicate entries); land the step 4a edit alone and nothing writes at all (the original defect,\\nnow with the fallback removed). Architect \\u00a72.2 notes they can land in one commit. They are two\\nhalves of one destination move against a single defect site, so they are one task.\\n\\n**Why T3 does not depend on T1 or T2.** The doctrine change cross-references\\n`subagent-contract/SKILL.md`'s `<result_destination>` clause, which already exists unchanged in the\\nworking tree. It does not quote or depend on any prose T1 or T2 writes. T1, T2 and T3 are fully\\nparallel; only T4 depends on all three.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"\",\"issue\":\"3276\",\"tasks\":[],\"source_path\":null,\"state\":\"drafting\",\"acceptance_criteria_structured\":[{\"criterion_id\":\"AC1-cv-writes-to-backend\",\"description\":\"contract-verification.md instructs the agent to write its finding via backlog_groom (AC1: violations reach a durable location with no human transcription)\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q 'backlog_groom' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC2-clean-result-recorded\",\"description\":\"contract-verification.md specifies an affirmative pre-resolved entry for the no-violations case, so silence never encodes 'clean' (AC2)\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q '\\\\[x\\\\] CONTRACT' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC3-sync-claim-removed\",\"description\":\"The line-151 synchronous-return override is gone (AC3)\",\"check_command\":\"! grep -q 'finding is your response' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC3-consumer-branch-removed\",\"description\":\"implement-feature step 4a no longer branches on a return value that never arrives\",\"check_command\":\"! grep -q 'If the contract-verification agent returns' plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC3-issue-number-threaded\",\"description\":\"contract-verification.md declares issue_number as a required input so it can address backlog_groom\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q 'issue_number' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC4-diagnostic-registers\",\"description\":\"groom/error.md's diagnostic agent registers findings as an artifact instead of returning them (AC4)\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q 'artifact_register' plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC4-decision-tree-reads-back\",\"description\":\"groom/error.md reads the diagnostic back before its Mermaid decision tree branches, making the Escalation branch reachable (AC4)\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q 'artifact_read' plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"doctrine-claim-removed\",\"description\":\"dispatch-contract/SKILL.md no longer authorizes 'finding is its response' as a valid result destination (Risk R2)\",\"check_command\":\"! grep -q 'whose finding is its response' plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"doctrine-selection-preserved\",\"description\":\"The true specialist-selection guidance survives the doctrine edit (architect \\u00a74.1)\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q 'dh roster or not' plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC5-no-sendmessage-grant\",\"description\":\"The unused SendMessage tool grant is revoked from contract-verification.md's frontmatter (architect \\u00a71.4)\",\"check_command\":\"! grep -q 'SendMessage' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC5-scope-boundary\",\"description\":\"AC5 / architect \\u00a76: no added line introduces TeamCreate, team-lead, or SendMessage \\u2014 #3250's scope is untouched\",\"check_command\":\"! git diff main -- plugins/development-harness | grep -qE '^\\\\+.*(TeamCreate|team-lead|SendMessage)'\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"subagent-contract-unchanged\",\"description\":\"architect \\u00a75: subagent-contract/SKILL.md is confirmed correct as-is and must carry zero changes\",\"check_command\":\"git diff --quiet main -- plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"}]}"}